The north parking lot will be repaved next week. Work will begin on Monday, September 9, and is expected to {{135}} by Thursday. During this time, the north lot will be closed to all vehicles.

Employees who usually park in the north lot should use the south lot {{136}}. Because the south lot has fewer spaces, we encourage staff to carpool or take public transportation if possible. {{137}}

We understand that this may cause some {{138}}, and we thank you for your patience.

Thank you for purchasing the AirPure 300 air purifier. To keep your unit running {{135}}, please follow these simple care instructions.

The filter should be replaced every six months. {{136}}, if you live in an area with heavy traffic or high levels of dust, you may need to replace it more often. Replacement filters can be ordered directly from our Web site.

Clean the outside of the unit regularly with a soft, dry cloth. Never use water or cleaning sprays, as these can {{137}} the electronic parts inside. {{138}}

Starting on Monday, April 15, all employees will be required to wear their new photo ID badges at all times while in the building. The new badges {{131}} at the security office on the first floor between 9:00 A.M. and 5:00 P.M. this week.

The new badges contain an electronic chip that will allow employees to enter the building and other restricted areas {{132}} having to sign in at the front desk. {{133}}

If your badge is lost or stolen, please report it to the security office {{134}}. A replacement badge will be issued within one business day.

FreshCart Market now delivers groceries to your door! Simply place your order on our Web site or mobile app, and choose a delivery time that is {{135}} for you. Deliveries are available seven days a week from 8:00 A.M. to 9:00 P.M.

Orders over $50 are delivered free of charge. For smaller orders, a fee of $4.99 {{136}}. {{137}}

All orders are packed with care to ensure that they arrive in perfect condition. {{138}}, frozen items are placed in insulated bags to keep them cold until they reach you.

At Lakeview Home Goods, we want you to be completely satisfied with your purchase. If you are not happy with an item, you may return it within 30 days of the purchase date for a full refund. Items must be unused and in their original packaging. A receipt or other proof of purchase is also {{139}}.

Refunds will be issued using the original method of payment. {{140}}, if you paid by credit card, the amount will be credited back to that card. {{141}}

Please note that certain items, such as mattresses and custom-made furniture, cannot be returned. Sale items may be exchanged {{142}} not refunded.

All meeting rooms at Norland Tech must now be reserved through the RoomFinder system on the company intranet. To book a room, log in with your employee ID and select the date and time of your meeting. The system will then {{143}} a list of rooms that are free at that time.

When choosing a room, please consider the size of your group. Small rooms are designed for up to four people, {{144}} large rooms can seat up to twenty. {{145}}

If your plans change, please cancel your reservation as soon as possible so that the room can be made available to {{146}}.

As part of our commitment to reducing waste, we are introducing a new recycling program next week. Blue bins for paper and green bins for plastic and cans will be placed in the kitchen on {{131}} floor.

Please make sure that items are clean and dry before you put them in the bins. Food waste should not be placed in the recycling bins, {{132}} it can contaminate other materials. {{133}}

We will track the amount of waste the office {{134}} each month and share the results with everyone. Thank you for helping us make our workplace more environmentally friendly.

Beginning on March 3, the Skyline Airport Shuttle will operate on a new schedule. Shuttles will now leave Central Station every 20 minutes, instead of every 30 minutes, between 5:00 A.M. and 11:00 P.M. {{135}}

Tickets cost $12 one way and can be purchased online or from the driver. Passengers {{136}} book online will receive a $2 discount. Please note that large luggage must be placed in the storage area at the back of the vehicle, and no more than two bags {{137}} per passenger.

We {{138}} for any inconvenience caused by the change and thank you for choosing Skyline.

Follow the steps below to connect your new Printwell X20 printer to your home network.

First, plug in the printer and turn it on. Wait until the green light {{143}} flashing before you continue. Next, download the Printwell app on your phone or tablet. {{144}}

Open the app and select "Add Printer." The app will search for printers {{145}} are nearby. When your printer appears on the screen, tap its name and enter your network password. If the connection is {{146}}, a message will appear, and you may begin printing.
